    "body": "## Summary\n- prevent deletion of attachments that already back a job expense claim\n- preserve the encrypted storage object as immutable financial evidence after claim creation\n- keep ordinary attachment deletion behavior unchanged for attachments that are not part of an expense audit trail\n- add regression coverage proving claimed receipts are neither soft-deleted nor removed from storage\n- document receipt-retention semantics in the expense model\n\n## Why\nThe receipt-backed expense flow merged in #106 made claims immutable, but the attachment delete path did not know whether an attachment had already entered the financial audit trail. A worker could therefore attempt to delete the evidence after creating a claim. This slice closes that lifecycle gap before exposing expense claims more broadly in the web UI.\n\n## Migration\nNo Flyway migration is required. `job_expense_claims.attachment_id` already records the evidence relationship; deletion is now blocked at the attachment service boundary.\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all required checks for the exact latest head are green. Any failure will be fixed on this same branch and rerun.",
