            "patch_url": "https://github.com/jedreekPrograms/dofast/pull/110.patch",
            "merged_at": "2026-08-29T09:24:08Z"
          },
          "body": "## Summary\n- add frontend API bindings for participant expense summaries and receipt-backed claims\n- show the protected expense budget, claimed/reimbursed/refunded totals and immutable claim history to job participants\n- let the assigned worker pair an eligible private receipt with an amount while the job is `IN_PROGRESS`\n- enforce immediate client-side remaining-budget feedback while keeping backend validation authoritative\n- mark claimed receipts as retained financial evidence and stop offering their delete action in the UI\n- document the end-to-end browser flow and privacy boundary\n\n## Why\nThe backend expense escrow introduced in #106 and receipt retention from #107 were production-capable, while #109 only exposed worker receipt upload. A worker still could not submit the actual reimbursement claim through the product UI. This slice closes that commercial gap without widening backend permissions or changing financial settlement semantics.\n\n## Migration\nNo Flyway migration is required. This consumes the existing V42 expense model and endpoints.\n\n## Validation\nDo not merge until all required workflow/check runs for the exact latest head complete successfully. Fix any failures on this branch and rerun before merge.",
